comments = 'On 2/27/2020, Sheppard Pratt Hospital contacted the agency for assistance. It was reported that Jason Benton age 16 was ready for discharge. His legal guardians, Janice Hadel and Howard Hadel were refusing to take him home. Jason had been hospitalized at SPH since 2/12/20. Jason’s diagnoses are DMDD, Anxiety, and Mild Intellectual, specific learning disorder with impairment in Reading, Written Expression, Mathematics, PTSD, Cannabis abuse, and ADHD. Jason was prescribed psychotropic medications and is compliant. There continue to be concerns of the affects of his Marijuana use while taking prescribed medications. Jason is adamant about continued use of Marijuana and suggests he will get a Marijuana card. Other behavioral concerns indicated are: Jason’s aggressive behaviors in the home. He has destroyed property, punched holes in the walls, and sent inappropriate pictures on social media. Jason was found stealing funds from Mrs. Hadel and other family members to pay for online profiles, self-harming behaviors, cutting, and suicidal ideation. Sheppard Pratt recommended a Diagnostic Center placement for Jason, however; he was not accepted at Arrow Diagnostic Center. Alternatively, Sheppard Pratt provided a recommendation for a therapeutic group home. Jason has had multiple inpatient hospitalizations at Franklin Square Hospital and Sheppard Pratt. He also attended the Sheppard Pratt Day School. His outpatient mental health providers were with Keypoint Health, therapist Caitlin Farha, and psychiatrist, Dr Arun, 410-938-3648, Lindsey Young, PRP in home services. Jason was accepted and placed at Greentree Adolescents Program on April 2, 2020.'
